TEST CLOSURE REPORT: Project "Everest" CBS Upgrade 
Date: October 24, 2023 | Version: 1.0 (Final) | Author: Test Manager
1. Executive Summary
This report formally concludes the testing phase for the Core Banking System (CBS) Upgrade. The objective was to modernize the back-end ledger, transaction processing, and interest calculation engines. Testing has met all planned exit criteria with 100% test execution and zero open defects at the time of closure.
Due to the critical nature of core ledger operations, the final recommendation is a Phased Rollout, starting with a pilot at the North Regional Hub before a nationwide release. 

2. Testing Scope & Strategy
Primary Focus: Back-end stability, transaction integrity, and General Ledger (GL) accuracy.
Key Modules: Account Management, Funds Transfer, Interest Accrual Engines, and End-of-Day (EOD) batch processing.
Environment Strategy: Utilized a Production Mirror environment. Testing was performed on a masked copy of live production data to ensure real-world data complexity while maintaining PII compliance.

